kosha wood

  -- natural composite: cellulose fibres (polymer) in lignin matrix.
  -- cellulose: (C6H10O5)n — linear glucose polymer. strong fibres.
  -- lignin: cross-linked aromatic polymer. binds cellulose, waterproofs.
  -- anisotropic: properties differ along and across the grain.
  --   strong along grain (fibres parallel to load).
  --   splits easily across grain (fibres separate).
  --
  -- properties:
  --   solid at room temperature
  --   thermal insulator (k ≈ 0.13 W/mK — air trapped in cells)
  --   coefficient of restitution: ~0.3-0.5 depending on species/hardness
  --   flammable: cellulose combustion at ~300°C ignition temperature
  --   biodegradable: enzymes (cellulase, lignase) break it down
  --   hygroscopic: absorbs moisture, swells and contracts
  --
  -- hardwoods (oak, teak, walnut) vs softwoods (pine, cedar, balsa).
  -- hardness range: balsa 0.1 Mohs equivalent, ebony 9.

